# Prefer local agents (budget vs CI)

**Default: local.** Omit Task `environment`, or set `"local"`. This studio’s Cursor budget is **effectively zero**. The local machine can run implement, tests, Bugbot, and Architect. Cloud is **not** a smarter model and is **not** an outage fallback.

## Cloud cost (always warn)

`environment: "cloud"` bills extra: VM + install + a **full agent per stage**. Ticket rewinds (Bugbot ↔ Architect) multiply that. **Warn before any cloud launch** — do not downplay it.

## When cloud can be worth it

Cloud is a **clean CI-like environment** (isolated clone, install, tests), not a better reviewer. That can matter for **expensive or involved** work (encryption/vault, schema migration, release builds, Windows exe packaging) because catching bugs in that loop is cheaper than shipping a broken installer.

If the ticket looks like that, **say the tradeoff once** (cost spike vs closer-to-CI coverage) and **stay local** until the human opts in. Do **not** auto-switch.

## Required to actually use cloud

Never set `environment: "cloud"` unless the **current user message** explicitly accepts the extra cost (e.g. “accept cloud cost” / “I accept the extra bill”).

“Do it in the cloud,” “not locally,” or “machine is slow” **without** that phrase → stay local, one-sentence cost warning, remind them they can opt in.

## Not reasons to go cloud

Machine feel, ticket length, “cloud is higher quality,” or watchdog/stuck recovery. Retry the **local** model chain. Do not use cloud to reach Opus or Sonnet.

